-> T26 Phase 3: `∪` between a Set and a Schema (or any combination involving
-> a Schema) can't collapse to a flat Set — a Schema's membership is open/
-> predicate-based. Produces a Value::Union: a discriminated union, resolved
-> the same way Set/Schema are (Status itself is one well-defined value).
Status = { "Success" } ∪ { tag = "Error", code ∈ Number }
assert Status ∈ Union

-> Narrowing `s ∈ Status` and resolving to the Set-shaped alternative.
s ∈ Status
s = "Success"
assert s = "Success"

-> A fresh variable resolving to the Schema-shaped alternative instead.
e ∈ Status
e = { tag = "Error", code = 500 }
assert e.tag = "Error"
assert e.code = 500

-> Once resolved, discriminating which alternative a value took is just
-> ordinary membership/type checks — no new mechanism needed.
if e ∈ Object {
    assert e.tag = "Error"
}
if e ∈ String {
    assert false
}
